IMPORT prelude

-- Poisons Act 1938 (Singapore) -- who may sell poisons and how (ss 5, 6, 8), the medicines exemption (s 7), keeping and storing
-- poisons (s 9), licences for medical practitioners (s 10(2)), penalties and liability of employers (s 16), the burden on a person
-- found with poisons (s 18(2)), sale to persons below 18 (s 19), composition (s 19A), the ceiling for offences under rules
-- (s 20(1)(o)), and a sample of the Poisons List in the Schedule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PA1938.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 9 of 2026 (in force 1 May 2026) and, in the Schedule, S 770/2025 shown. THE ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS IN THE DEPOSIT IS SHIFTED
-- BY ONE against the body (it lists "19A. Prohibition of sale to persons below 18 years"); this encoding follows the BODY, where
-- that prohibition is s 19 and composition is s 19A. The body's own cross-references (s 2 to s 4, s 16 to ss 7 and 8, s 8 to s 6)
-- are consistent with the body numbering.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a seller, pharmacist,
-- doctor or holder of poisons meets. Not encoded: the licensing officers and register (ss 4, 12, 13), search and warrants (s 14),
-- the Minister's exemption orders (s 15), the Minister's power to change the List (s 3(2)), forfeiture (s 16(2)), jurisdiction and
-- consent to prosecute (ss 17, 18(1)), fees (ss 19B, 19C), the rule-making heads in s 20 other than (o), and any rules made under
-- the Act (none retrieved). Licence terms and periods are left to the licence and to rules.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Poisons Act 1938 -- sale, keeping and penalties`

§§ `5 -- the licence requirement`

-- s 5: "No person shall without a licence from a licensing officer import, possess for sale, sell or offer for sale any poison."
-- s 18(2): "the burden of proving that any poison found in the possession of the accused was not kept for sale shall be upon the
-- accused."
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `importing`
    `possessing for sale`
    `selling`
    `offering for sale`
    `possessing for own use`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing needs a licence` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `possessing for own use` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing without a licence contravenes s 5` IF
    `the dealing needs a licence` `the dealing` AND (NOT `holds a licence`)

GIVEN `found in possession` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proved it was not kept for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the poison is treated as kept for sale` IF
    `found in possession` AND (NOT `the accused proved it was not kept for sale`)

§§ `6 and 8 -- conditions of every sale`

-- s 6(1)(a): no sale unless (i) the seller "is licensed under this Act to sell poisons"; (ii) in accordance with the licence and its
-- conditions; (iii) on the premises specified in the licence; (iv) "by or under the personal supervision of the person named in the
-- licence"; and (v) "by or under the personal supervision of a pharmacist".
-- s 6(1)(b): no sale "by way of wholesale dealing except to a person licensed under this Act to sell that poison".
-- s 6(2): the container must be labelled with (a) the name of the poison; (b) for a preparation, the proportion of poison to total
-- ingredients; (c) the word "Poison" or other prescribed indication; (d) the seller's name and the address of the premises.
-- s 6(3) (subject to rules relaxing it): (a) the buyer must be known to the seller or a pharmacist employed there, or introduced by
-- someone known to the seller; (b) the seller "shall not deliver it until" an entry is made in a book (date, names and addresses,
-- substance, quantity, stated purpose) and (ii) the purchaser and any introducer "have affixed their signatures to that entry".
-- s 8: "nothing in section 6(1)(a)(v), (2) and (3) shall extend to" (a) wholesale sales; (b) sales "to be exported from Singapore to
-- a place other than Malaysia"; (c) sales to a medical practitioner, registered dentist or veterinary surgeon for his profession;
-- (d) for an approved hospital, dispensary or similar institution; (e) for a Government department or local authority; (f) to a
-- person or institution for scientific education or research; (g) by licensed persons to a person who needs it for trade or
-- business (or for the medical treatment of his employees under written law).
-- s 8 relaxes only the pharmacist, labelling and record rules. The licence, premises and named-person rules in s 6(1)(a)(i)-(iv),
-- and the wholesale rule in s 6(1)(b), still bind.
DECLARE Buyer IS ONE OF
    `a member of the public`
    `a buyer for resale`
    `an exporter to a place other than Malaysia`
    `an exporter to Malaysia`
    `a doctor, dentist or vet for the profession`
    `an approved hospital or dispensary`
    `a Government department or local authority`
    `a school or research body for education or research`
    `a business needing it for its trade`

GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Buyer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8 relaxes the sale` IF
    CONSIDER `the buyer`
    WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an exporter to Malaysia` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Sale HAS
    `buyer` IS A Buyer
    `the seller is licensed to sell poisons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in accordance with the licence and its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the licensed premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under the supervision of the person named in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under the supervision of a pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyer is licensed to sell that poison` IS A BOOLEAN
    `labelled with the name of the poison` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the poison is in a preparation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `labelled with the proportion of poison` IS A BOOLEAN
    `labelled Poison` IS A BOOLEAN
    `labelled with the seller's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyer is known or introduced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered in the poisons book before delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is signed by the buyer and any introducer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence conditions of s 6(1)(a)(i) to (iv) are met` IF
        `the sale`'s `the seller is licensed to sell poisons`
    AND `the sale`'s `in accordance with the licence and its conditions`
    AND `the sale`'s `on the licensed premises`
    AND `the sale`'s `under the supervision of the person named in the licence`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wholesale rule of s 6(1)(b) is met` IF
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `buyer`
    WHEN `a buyer for resale` THEN `the sale`'s `the buyer is licensed to sell that poison`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the labelling of s 6(2) is complete` IF
        `the sale`'s `labelled with the name of the poison`
    AND ((NOT `the sale`'s `the poison is in a preparation`) OR `the sale`'s `labelled with the proportion of poison`)
    AND `the sale`'s `labelled Poison`
    AND `the sale`'s `labelled with the seller's name and address`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer and record rules of s 6(3) are met` IF
        `the sale`'s `the buyer is known or introduced`
    AND `the sale`'s `entered in the poisons book before delivery`
    AND `the sale`'s `the entry is signed by the buyer and any introducer`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale complies with s 6` IF
        `the licence conditions of s 6(1)(a)(i) to (iv) are met` `the sale`
    AND `the wholesale rule of s 6(1)(b) is met` `the sale`
    AND (    `section 8 relaxes the sale` (`the sale`'s `buyer`)
         OR (    `the sale`'s `under the supervision of a pharmacist`
             AND `the labelling of s 6(2) is complete` `the sale`
             AND `the buyer and record rules of s 6(3) are met` `the sale`))

§§ `7 -- medicines supplied by practitioners and pharmacists`

-- s 7(1): "nothing in section 6 shall apply" to (a) a medicine supplied by a medical practitioner for treating his own patients;
-- (b) by a registered dentist for dental treatment of his own patients; (c) by a veterinary surgeon for animal treatment; (d) a
-- medicine "dispensed by a licensed pharmacist on the premises specified in his licence"; or (e) a poison forming part of a
-- medicine, "except a patent or proprietary medicine", supplied by a licensed pharmacist on his licensed premises -- "if the
-- requirements contained in subsections (2), (3) and (4) are satisfied".
-- (2): labelled with the supplier's name and address and a serial or other identification number or mark.
-- (3): entered in a book "On the day on which the medicine is supplied or dispensed or, if that is not reasonably practicable, on the
-- day next following that day". (4) relaxes the content of the entry for a repeat prescription, not its timing; it is not modelled.
-- (5): a medicine supplied or dispensed "by a pharmacist or medical practitioner" must have been compounded by or under his direct and
-- personal supervision. (No such requirement is written for a dentist or a vet.)
-- s 7(5) is not one of the conditions listed in s 7(1) ("subsections (2), (3) and (4)"). Treating it as a further condition of the
-- exemption is an INFERENCE from its wording ("must have been"); the text does not say what follows if it is not met.
DECLARE Supplier IS ONE OF
    `a medical practitioner treating his own patient`
    `a registered dentist treating his own patient`
    `a veterinary surgeon treating an animal`
    `a licensed pharmacist dispensing on his licensed premises`
    `a licensed pharmacist supplying a medicine containing a poison on his licensed premises`
    `a licensed pharmacist supplying away from his licensed premises`
    `a medical practitioner supplying someone else's patient`

DECLARE Supply HAS
    `supplier` IS A Supplier
    `a patent or proprietary medicine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `labelled with supplier, address and identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after supply when entered in the book` IS A NUMBER
    `entry on the day was not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `compounded under the supplier's personal supervision` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply is of a kind s 7(1) covers` IF
    CONSIDER `the supply`'s `supplier`
    WHEN `a medical practitioner treating his own patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered dentist treating his own patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a veterinary surgeon treating an animal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed pharmacist dispensing on his licensed premises` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed pharmacist supplying a medicine containing a poison on his licensed premises`
        THEN NOT `the supply`'s `a patent or proprietary medicine`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the book entry is in time` IF
        `the supply`'s `days after supply when entered in the book` EQUALS 0
    OR  (    `the supply`'s `days after supply when entered in the book` EQUALS 1
         AND `the supply`'s `entry on the day was not reasonably practicable`)

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(5) compounding applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the supply`'s `supplier`
    WHEN `a registered dentist treating his own patient` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a veterinary surgeon treating an animal` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 takes the supply outside s 6` IF
        `the supply is of a kind s 7(1) covers` `the supply`
    AND `the supply`'s `labelled with supplier, address and identification number`
    AND `the book entry is in time` `the supply`
    AND ((NOT `s 7(5) compounding applies` `the supply`) OR `the supply`'s `compounded under the supplier's personal supervision`)

§§ `9 -- keeping poisons`

-- s 9(1): "No person whether licensed under this Act or not shall knowingly keep or have in his possession or under his control any
-- poison otherwise than" (a) in an unbroken case or package as received from the manufacturer; or (b) in a receptacle "distinctly
-- labelled with the name of the substance contained therein and bearing some distinction or mark indicating that it contains poison".
-- (2): a person proved to have kept it "shall be deemed to have done so knowingly unless the contrary is proved by him".
-- There is no exception for a household or for a medicine lawfully bought; s 16(1) excepts only ss 7 and 8 acts.
GIVEN `in the unbroken manufacturer's package` IS A BOOLEAN, `labelled with the substance's name` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `marked as poison` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved he did not know` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping the poison contravenes s 9(1)` IF
        (NOT `in the unbroken manufacturer's package`)
    AND (NOT (`labelled with the substance's name` AND `marked as poison`))
    AND (NOT `proved he did not know`)

-- s 9(3): poison kept "for sale or for dispensing purposes" only (a) in the unbroken manufacturer's package; (b) in a vessel secured
-- differently from those holding non-poisonous substances; (c) in a vessel "readily distinguishable by touch"; or (d) in a room or
-- cupboard "under lock and key set apart" for dangerous substances.
DECLARE Storage IS ONE OF
    `the unbroken manufacturer's package`
    `a vessel secured differently from non-poisons`
    `a vessel distinguishable by touch`
    `a locked room or cupboard set apart for dangerous substances`
    `an ordinary shelf bottle`

GIVEN `the storage` IS A Storage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the storage is permitted for stock kept for sale or dispensing` IF
    CONSIDER `the storage`
    WHEN `an ordinary shelf bottle` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `10(2) -- licences for medical practitioners`

-- s 10(2): "No licence shall be issued to a medical practitioner other than a licence authorising him to import, possess and sell
-- poisons by retail in connection with his own practice or with a practice or partnership in which every member is a medical
-- practitioner."
DECLARE `Doctor's licence` IS ONE OF
    `retail for his own practice`
    `retail for an all-doctor partnership`
    `retail for a partnership with a non-doctor`
    `wholesale dealing`

GIVEN `the licence sought` IS A `Doctor's licence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be issued to a medical practitioner` IF
    CONSIDER `the licence sought`
    WHEN `retail for his own practice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `retail for an all-doctor partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `16 -- penalties and who is liable`

-- s 16(1) (as amended by Act 9 of 2026): any person who contravenes the Act, "except insofar as his act comes within one of the
-- exemptions made by sections 7 and 8", is liable to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years or both.
-- s 20(1)(o): rules may make a contravention punishable by a fine not exceeding $20,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years.
-- Terms are given in months.
DECLARE Source IS ONE OF
    `the Act`
    `rules made under the Act`

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `the Act` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `the Act` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 24

-- s 16(4): an agent or employee who, in the course of employment, does or omits an act that would be an offence by the employer
-- "shall be guilty of that offence"; and the principal or employer is "deemed to be guilty" where it is proved the act or omission
-- was committed "with the consent or connivance of, or is attributable to any neglect on the part of" the employer.
GIVEN `in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is guilty` IF
    `in the course of employment`

GIVEN `in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the employer's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attributable to the employer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is deemed guilty` IF
    `in the course of employment` AND (`with the employer's consent or connivance` OR `attributable to the employer's neglect`)

§§ `19 -- sale to persons below 18`

-- s 19(1): "No poison shall be sold to any person below 18 years of age." (2): fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 5 years or both. (3): "a sufficient defence" that the seller "had reasonable cause to believe that the person to whom
-- the sale was made was above the age of 18 years".
-- s 19 carries its own penalty; the ss 7 and 8 exemptions are written for s 6 and s 16(1), not for s 19.
GIVEN `age of the buyer` IS A NUMBER, `reasonable cause to believe the buyer was above 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is an offence under s 19` IF
    `age of the buyer` LESS THAN 18 AND (NOT `reasonable cause to believe the buyer was above 18`)

§§ `19A -- composition`

-- s 19A(1) (inserted by Act 9 of 2026): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for a sum "not exceeding
-- the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) $5,000.
-- (2): on payment, "no further proceedings are to be taken".
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the prescribed maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the lower of` (`the prescribed maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
    ELSE 0

§§ `3 and the Schedule -- the Poisons List (a sample)`

-- s 3(1): "The substances specified in the Poisons List shall be deemed to be poisons". The List runs to nearly 2,000 lines of the deposit; a few
-- entries are sampled. Present: "Codeine; its esters and ethers; ...", "Ibuprofen", "Nicotine; its salts; ...", "Warfarin; its
-- salts", "Sildenafil; its salts; ...". Conditional: "Xylometazoline; its salts; when contained in eye preparations"; "Urea, when
-- contained in preparations intended for human consumption, except external preparations containing not more than 10% of urea".
-- Paracetamol and aspirin (acetylsalicylic acid) do not appear in the deposited List (a text search found neither).
DECLARE Substance IS ONE OF
    `codeine`
    `ibuprofen`
    `nicotine`
    `warfarin`
    `sildenafil`
    `paracetamol`
    `aspirin`
    `xylometazoline`
    `urea`

GIVEN `the substance` IS A Substance, `in an eye preparation` IS A BOOLEAN, `for human consumption` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an external preparation with at most 10% urea` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is a poison` IF
    CONSIDER `the substance`
    WHEN `paracetamol` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `aspirin` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `xylometazoline` THEN `in an eye preparation`
    WHEN `urea` THEN `for human consumption` AND (NOT `an external preparation with at most 10% urea`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE
